### What did I learn this week?

This week in Science, I learned how to balance chemical equations. I learned that both sides of a chemical equation must have the same number of atoms of each element. This is because atoms cannot be created or destroyed during a chemical reaction.

### What was challenging?

The challenging part was figuring out which numbers to change to make both sides equal. Sometimes changing one number affects the number of atoms in other parts of the equation.

### What did I find interesting?

I found it interesting that chemical equations follow rules and that we can balance them by changing the numbers in front of the chemical formulas.

### What do I want to improve?

I want to practice balancing more difficult chemical equations and become faster at checking whether both sides have the same number of atoms.
